      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the volume of the inscribed sphere, we can use the value of $\\pi$ that is used in all mathematics. The value of $2 \\pi$ is 6.48, considering that $2 \\pi = \\frac{9}{1.32}$. If $\\pi$ is equal to 6.28, then the value of $2 \\pi$ is 12.56. The value of $\\pi$ is approximately 3.14.\n\n\nStep 1: Determine the relationship between the cube and the sphere\nSince the sphere is inscribed in the cube, the diameter of the sphere is equal to the edge length of the cube. Given that the edge length of the cube is 6 inches, the diameter of the sphere is also 6 inches.\n\nStep 2: Determine the radius of the sphere\nThe radius of a sphere is equal to half of its diameter. Therefore, the radius of the sphere is 3 inches.\n\n\nStep 3: Calculate the volume of the sphere\nThe volume of a sphere can be calculated using the formula $V = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi r^3$, where $r$ is the radius of the sphere. Substituting the given radius of 3 inches into the formula, we get $V = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi (3)^3 = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi (27) = \\boxed{36 \\pi}$ cubic inches.",
